{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1515239-mechanic-to-communicate-with-spirits-without-spirit-speech","id":1515239,"title":"Mechanic to communicate with spirits without Spirit Speech","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-16T07:07:27-07:00","id":1515239,"title":"Mechanic to communicate with spirits without Spirit Speech","content":"I remember reading somewhere in one of the W20 books, I can't remember which one, that there's a mechanic for trying to understand a spirit, and for trying to 'speak their language', doing it manually with actions, body language and sounds. An Attribute + Ability roll, I couldn't even swear if it was Enigmas or Occult or something else.<br /> <br /> If anyone has any luck finding the rule I'm thinking of I'd be really thankful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T08:51:29-07:00","id":1515253,"title":"","content":"I can't seem to find it in W20 or Revised. Both imply that spirits either speak human tongues or you need Spirit Speech to commune with them, which does not gel with what I remember. I've taken a look in the Umbra books as well and I cannot seem a reference to it. I'm 99% sure it was Enigmas and that you could use other skills to communicate with certain spirits - i.e. mathematics for weaver spirits or performance for music spirits?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":".  Typo 06-16-2023, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T09:33:39-07:00","id":1515259,"title":"","content":"The Spriits actually able to speak Garou (or any other language really) but usually choose <i>not to</i><br /> They are like Star Wars' Hutts, who are fluent in many languages but always use a protocol droid and expects to either learn their language or negotiate from a disadvantageous situation...<br /> Why?<br /> It is a bit of a power play<br /> Similar with the Spirits<br /> Spirits are not the besties of the Garou - think about it, the Garou suposedly are the Claws and Fangs of Gaia, Earth Mother's favorite and chosen race, superior to everyone... yet spirits not really rush to them to teahc them gifts, secrets, be their Fetish-fuel and so on, even in the middle of the War fo Gaia!<br /> <br /> King Albrecht couldn't even speak to spirits without a packmate to do it for him!<br /> <br /> Learning and using the Gift, the Garou actually humbles himself in a sense and humility from a Garou something the Spirits love<br /> The Gift allows the Garou to communicate with a spirits on its own tounge. The Garou is thus able to address them whether they wish to be adddressed or not. Of course, nothing prevents the spirit from ignoring the Werewolf or leaving...<br /> Once learned, this Gift allows the Garou to understand the communication of spirits intuitively. Particularly alien spirits may be difficult \u2014 or, in the case of many Banes, outright painful \u2014 to understand.<br /> <br /> Now lest wander in to half houserule, half &quot;the rules nowehere said <i>you can't do it</i>&quot; and other such area:<br /> In theory? IF a Garou learns the language of Spirits she wouldn' need this &quot;universal translator&quot;<br /> Since they are Half-spirits I usually let my players - if anyone bothers - to learn as a language IF a Spirit or anyone willing to teahc them and they willing to learn<br /> I treat the Gift as a subtitle during a movie<br /> There is a HUGE difference between readin the subtitle and understanding the language after all<br /> <br /> A bit like in the old joke:<br /> <br /> Jose had robbed a bank in Texas and fled south across the Rio Grande with the Texas Rangers in hot pursuit. They caught up with him in a town in Old Mexico, only to discover that Jose spoke no English and none of the pursuers spoke any Spanish. They drafted one of the locals \u2013 the school teacher \u2013 to act as a translator.<br /> \u201cTell Jose that he must tell us where he has hidden the loot from the bank robbery.\u201d<br /> \u201cThe gringos say to ask where you have hidden the loot.\u201d<br /> \u201cTell the gringos I will never tell them.\u201d<br /> \u201cJose says he will never tell you.\u201d<br /> The Rangers pull out their six-guns, cock them, and point them at Jose.<br /> \u201cTell Jose if he does not tell us where he has hidden the loot, we will kill him.\u201d<br /> \u201cThe gringos say if you do not tell them where you have hidden the loot they will kill you.\u201d<br /> Jose begins to tremble with fear.<br /> \u201cI buried it by the old oak tree on the other side of the bridge.\u201d<br /> The teacher nods<br /> <i>\u201cJose says he is not afraid to die.\u201d <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></i>\u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T12:27:57-07:00","id":1515282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1515239-mechanic-to-communicate-with-spirits-without-spirit-speech?p=1515259#post1515259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Spriits actually able to speak Garou (or any other language really) but usually choose <i>not to</i>\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I usually interpret this to mean that some spirits are capable (or willing) of communicating through the Garou Tongue, but not all. (Although I do think there is a case to make that all spirits can understand all forms of language, but as you say choose not to do so).<br /> <br /> I typically say that the most important spirits to that individual Garou will deign to use the Garou Tongue on certain occasions. Pack totems would probably do so (though this is best done by purchasing the appropriate power in the Totem background description). Their direct Ancestor spirits, the Caern totem of the sept the Garou belongs to, as would certain major spirits of one's tribal totem, and maybe some Lunes especially during their more mercurial phases. That does not mean they necessarily would do so, but these spirits would often have need to successfully communicate certain things to closely allied Garou and would not necessarily force them to use a Theurge to do the translating. And if there is enough of a chiminage relationship, this may even become routine. At the same time, a spirit who is willing to use the Garou Tongue once or more to accomplish his own ends could also completely ignore the same characters speaking in the Garou Tongue later on, forcing them to find someone who knows spirit speech.<br /> <br /> Other spirits, even though nominally allied to the Garou as Gaian spirits, would not necessarily do so. Even spirits within the spirit brood of the tribal incarna may prefer the more formal way of communication for the reasons you mentioned. And there are plenty of other Gaian spirits that would be antagonistic or even hostile at some level - spirit broods that have rivalry like the Fenris and Pegasus, or spirits more closely aligned to one of the Changing Breeds. They simply won't use the Garou Tongue.<br /> <br /> I tend to use the more alien spirits like elementals, triatic spirits, and enigmatic spirits as never using the Garou Tongue.<br /> <br /> STs (and players) often have needs when they must speak to the spirit even though there is no one in the scene who could reasonably do so (no Theurge with spirit speech, no pack totem nearby to &quot;translate&quot; on behalf of the Garou). So I think it is OK for STs to find runarounds provided they make sense in the setting. But it would be a bad ST to invalidate the utility of a Theurge when such things are supposed to be their time to shine. The ST just needs to find justification for some wriggle room and some important exceptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}